 "notes": [
  "Table 2 groups the lists into electoral unions; the party keys are the leaf ('of which') columns, so they sum to the valid total. Union totals printed: Kekkonen union (skdl+tpsl+sdp+ml+kekkonen_union_rkp+kekkonen_union_ind) 1 152 700; Swedish People's Party union (rkp_kekkonen+rkp_vennamo+rkp_virkkunen) 112 947; National Coalition union (kok+kok_ind) 438 801.",
  "ml = Keskustapuolue (Center Party). kekkonen_union_rkp = Swedish People's Party candidates inside the Kekkonen electoral union (Helsinki only); kekkonen_union_ind = independents (Puolueettomat) in the Kekkonen union. rkp_kekkonen / rkp_vennamo / rkp_virkkunen = adherents of Kekkonen / Vennamo / Virkkunen within the Swedish People's Party electoral union. smp = Vennamo's electoral union, footnoted as the Finnish Rural Party (Suomen Maaseudun Puolue) and independents. kok_ind = independents in the National Coalition union. lkp = the Liberal People's Party electoral union, which nominated Kekkonen. written = written lists (Kirjoitetut listat).",
  "Footnote 1: the Liberal People's Party union figure for Helsinki (18 865) includes 94 votes for an independent candidate.",
  "Footnote 2: the Virkkunen adherents figure for Helsinki (24 988) includes 105 votes for a candidate of the Independence Party (Itsenäisyyspuolue).",
  "Footnote 4: Åland's 3 910 votes (shown in the Swedish People's Party union total and its Kekkonen adherents column) are for Ahvenanmaan Kokoomus (Åländsk Samling), the only list in Åland, which supported Kekkonen; its 1 elector is printed in the same column of table 8 (footnoted likewise).",
  "Table 1 footnote: the national voters total (2 049 002) and Uusimaa's (185 332) include 111 persons whose sex and commune are unknown. Table 1 voters are counted by place of registration, so they differ from the ballots in table 2.",
  "Table 8 has no column for kekkonen_union_rkp or rkp_vennamo (no electors). Of the 300 electors, 201 were Kekkonen adherents, 33 Vennamo adherents and 66 Virkkunen adherents; 52 were women.",
  "Constituencies unchanged from 1962; seats were increased by two in Helsinki and Uusimaa and by one in Häme South, and reduced by one in Mikkeli, North Karelia, Central Finland, Vaasa and Oulu.",
  "Polling days 15 and 16 January 1968. The volume has English, not French, headings, so fr is null."
 ],
